  "analysis": "Both responses address the core requirements—verification layer, maintenance windows, CI constraints, dual approvals, SSL rotation, and immutable logs. PKD adds concrete actions like a shadow‑mode run, automatic retry of the flaky test, and a rollback script that creates a corrective retraction entry to work around the immutable schema, which directly solves the requester’s concern about irreversible false incidents. LXQ provides a solid plan but its rollback relies on a feature‑flag flip and mentions a full migration only as a high‑severity step, offering less concrete mitigation for the immutable‑log issue.",
